Task: Puppy visibility correction (FR7, AC8) — Phase 5, found in the gate

Summary
-------
Two independent defects in the shipped lost-puppy mission, both found by
inspection after the Phase 5 walkthrough raised the question "what if the pup
is behind a building?":

1. SPOT AUTHORING. `puppySpots`' only written rule was "on a non-road tile the
   town's pathing can reach". Two of four spots failed worse than that:
   - `spot-garden` (tile 2,3 offset -0.3/+0.35) sat inside house-4's lot.
   - `spot-verge` (tile 1,4 offset -0.35/0) sat inside house-5's lot.
   Houses fill up to HOUSE_LOT_FIT (0.86) of their lot, so half-extents run
   ~0.29-0.43 against those deltas. The pup is PUPPY_HEIGHT = 0.2, i.e. a
   20 cm dog inside/against a wall.
   `spot-garden` was the severe one: hemmed in by adjacent houses whose gaps
   (1.0 pitch - 0.86 fill = 0.14) are narrower than the car (CAR_RADIUS 0.26,
   diameter 0.52), the closest legal car position to it was > 1.3 away, well
   outside PICKUP_RADIUS 0.6. The pup could never be collected, and because
   `isBusy()` stays true for a non-idle mission, the town's busy gate would
   hold shut for the rest of the session - a soft-lock, not a cosmetic bug.

2. OCCLUSION. The paw print is the mission's signpost and the only marker in
   the game at ground level (PAW_BASE_HEIGHT 0.06); the order cone and the
   heart both float at MARKER_BASE_HEIGHT 1.7, documented as "above a Kenney
   house roof". The camera is a fixed orthographic view along
   CAMERA_DIRECTION (1, sqrt2, 1) - 35.3 degrees of elevation, not the "~45"
   the comment claims - so a house hides ground up to ~1.41x its height on the
   side away from the camera, and a 0.2-tall pup hides behind a tree at the
   distance the authored spots place it. The design says "the pup hides, the
   paw print is the signpost"; the signpost was the one thing that could be
   hidden, which breaks the pillar that every concept is conveyed by a visible
   icon.

Approach (approved by the track owner: fix inside this track, FR7/AC8)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Data half: two new pure, tested predicates in `puppySpots` -
`isClearOfHouses` and `isScoopable` - measured against the HOUSE_LOT_FIT cap
rather than the mounted art, so any spot that passes them passes whatever the
renderer draws, including after an art swap. `isScoopable` samples rings at
four radii (32 angles each) for a legal car position within PICKUP_RADIUS.
The two lot spots moved to the kerb of the street each house faces;
`spot-garden` -> house-4's east kerb (2,3 offset 0.48/0.25), `spot-verge` ->
house-5's south verge (1,4 offset 0.2/0.48). The two park hides stay, where
hiding is genuinely honest (tree and dumpster between pup and camera).

Rendering half: `createPawMarker` now sets `depthTest: false`,
`depthWrite: false` and an explicit render order on its meshes, so the print
draws after the scene and over whatever the pup is behind. One shared material
per marker, so the change is three lines of configuration. The heart keeps
normal depth testing - it is above the roofline - and a new test pins that
asymmetry so the exemption cannot spread by accident.

